ar beyond this run's budget. Proposed well-posed alternative: use a potential validated for alkane intermolecular energies (e.g. a molecular MLIP such as MACE-OFF, or a TraPPE-UA/L-OPLS classical force field). First recover the measured Tm of n-octadecane (301.0 +/- 0.7 K) or n-hexadecane (291.0 +/- 1.0 K) from /data/calibration/tier1.json with the same solid-liquid interface coexistence protocol (NPT, about 100 molecules, at least 2 ns per temperature, bracketing temperatures 2-5 K apart). Then run eicosane (measured 310.0 +/- 1.0 K, used only as an a-posteriori check) and report the bracket half-width plus the validation offset as the uncertainty.\",\n \"details\": {\"model\": \"MACE-MPA-0 medium (mace-torch 0.3.15, float64)\",\n   \"s22_methane_dimer_kJmol\": {\"mace_mpa0\": -46.53, \"reference_ccsdt\": -2.2},\n   \"s22_ethene_dimer_kJmol\": {\"mace_mpa0\": -30.84, \"reference_ccsdt\": -6.3},\n   \"eicosane_parallel_dimer_scan_kJmol\": {\"3.8\": -250.2, \"4.0\": -265.4, \"4.2\": -253.2, \"4.5\": -216.3, \"5.0\": -144.6, \"6.0\": -47.2, \"7.0\": -1.3, \"9.0\": 0.0},\n   \"eicosane_dsubH_exp_kJmol\": {\"value\": 170.4, \"source\": \"NIST Chemistry WebBook C112958 Mask=4 (Morawetz 1972)\"},\n   \"scripts\": [\"/work/scripts/dimer.py\", \"/work/scripts/methane.py\"],\n   \"caveat\": \"Eicosane dimer geometry is idealized and unrelaxed, so the scan is semi-quantitative; the S22 test uses reference geometries and is the decisive validation.\"}}\nEOF\n./board post run_report @/tmp/rr.json --parent $CID; ./board show | tail -5","description":"Post candidate and refused run report"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":341,"cache_read_input_tokens":29385,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":341,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":16,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],